issue_body:
Tracking down another bit of difference between rust and python.

Given the following FEA,

```fea
languagesystem DFLT dflt;
languagesystem latn NLD;

feature locl {

    script latn;
    language NLD;
    lookup one {
        sub a by b;
    } one;

    script latn;
    language NLD;
    lookup two {
        sub x by z;
    } two;
} locl;
```

What is the expected behaviour?

- makeotf errors `ERROR: [line    14 char  14] language-specific behavior already specified`.
- fontmake produces a feature that only includes lookup two (basically it overwrites lookup one?)
- fea-rs produces a feature that includes both lookups.

Given that this is taken from a real-world example (FEA generated by Glyphs.app) I think we _do_ want to compile it, and in that case it looks to me like the intention is to include both lookups. Does anyone else see this differently?

